   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "target (on Documentary Story): YouTube video (16:9) or Instagram reel (9:16, about 30 s, at most 40; 4-6 photos work best).\n\n3 to 10 photos. Upload a photo into each Photo node (file_1 ... file_10 are placeholders). Fewer photos: delete any Photo nodes you don't need (keep at least 3).\n\nname: optional, what or who it is (e.g. 'Eurasian blue tit'); used as true and to look up its facts. note: optional, what is happening.\n\nmood: the tone of the narration, the voice, the music and the intro label. custom_style: your own tone.\n\nThe video: an intro collage with the story's title, the photos with transitions (transition: mix or one kind; fade: their length) and subtitles, and a follow card at the end. Put your @handle in Ken Burns Video (handle) and in Social Post. The narrator's last line is written by the story; Narrate Storyboard's outro replaces it ('-' = none).\n\nSocial Post: for a reel an Instagram caption, 5 hashtags, key phrases and alt text; for YouTube a title, description, tags and 3 hashtags. In the box below it.\nThumbnail: the sharpest, most colourful photo with the story's hook (photo: pick one; headline: your own text).\n\nStored files: menu Documentary → Stored files."
   ]
  }
